@startuml error-taxonomy
title Error taxonomy — which failure produces which MawaqitError
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

component "transport" as NET #FFF6DD
component "status check (before body read)" as ST #FFF6DD
component "body handling" as BODY #FFF6DD
component "calendar extraction" as CAL #FFF6DD

component "Http(reqwest)" as HTTP #FFE1E1
component "Parse" as PARSE #FFE1E1
component "MosqueNotFound" as MNF #FFE1E1
component "Api{status, url}" as API #FFE1E1
component "ConfDataNotFound" as CDNF #FFE1E1
component "NoCalendar" as NC #FFE1E1
component "InvalidMonth(u32)" as IM #FFE1E1
component "Compact(CompactError)\nMQTC load/pack failures: InvalidMagic · UnsupportedVersion\nBufferTooSmall · ChecksumMismatch · InvalidDate\nTimeOutOfRange · DeltaOverflow · IqamaOffsetOverflow\nTooManyDays" as COMPACT #FFE1E1

NET --> HTTP : connect refused / reset
NET --> HTTP : 30s timeout
NET --> PARSE : non-UTF-8 body
NET --> PARSE : body > 1 MiB cap
ST --> MNF : 404
ST --> API : other !2xx — incl. 3xx:\nredirects never followed (F1)
BODY --> PARSE : search: not a JSON array\n(one bad element)
BODY --> CDNF : page: no "confData =" assignment\nor unbalanced literal
BODY --> PARSE : page: literal not JSON
BODY --> PARSE : times < 5 strings
CAL --> NC : calendar missing/empty
CAL --> IM : month ∉ 1..=12
CAL --> PARSE : row would surface non-HH:MM\n(F4: day rejected whole)
CAL --> PARSE : row shape ≠ 5/6 (+/− shuruq col)
CAL --> NC : today's day missing

note as N1
  Semantic groupings — transient: Http, Api (5xx/429) → retry with
  backoff (examples/error_recovery.rs). Terminal: MosqueNotFound,
  InvalidMonth → caller error. Contract drift / hostile:
  ConfDataNotFound, Parse, NoCalendar, Compact → do not hammer; the
  snapshot fallback engages for conf_data.

  Fallback interaction: conf_data / conf_data_dated wrap the whole
  fetch — ANY variant here triggers the snapshot fallback when a disk
  cache is configured; the original error only surfaces if no snapshot
  loads. search_mosques has no fallback (cheap, user-initiated).
end note
@enduml
